⚡🇵🇱The Polish prosecution has stated that there is no evidence of an ideological motive in the Krakow attack, in which 24-year-old Michał Oksiński killed 6 people and injured another 16. Spokesperson Przemysław Nowak clarified that the motive remains to be determined.

 The Minister of the Interior had initially hypothesized a possible influence from the far right. The symbols found on the clothing the killer was wearing at the time of the attack are still under analysis. The attacker died in the hospital after being shot by the police.

